{
 "_readme": [
  "Where every OCRed work actually came from. One row per work slug under",
  "data/ocr_staging/.",
  "",
  "Why this file exists: on 18 Sep 2026 a Sarvam batch for 11 works could not be",
  "dispatched, because NOTHING in any repo recorded which PDF each work had been",
  "OCRed from. Not the staging JSON, not data/ocr_staging/index.json, not the",
  "branch commit messages, not ParaBuddhi. The URLs had to be re-derived from the",
  "scanned title pages and re-proved one by one. Do not stage OCR output without",
  "adding its row here.",
  "",
  "verified_by: 'page-count' means the source PDF was downloaded and its page",
  "count compared against the pages already staged. That check is what caught",
  "bhagavata_saroddhara: the obvious archive.org hit is a DIFFERENT edition of",
  "the same work (560 pages, Gajendragada Shyamaraya) and would have produced a",
  "Sarvam run that silently disagreed with Vision on every single page.",
  "",
  "pdf_url is built as archive.org/download/<item>/<url-quoted file>.",
  "",
  "language_blocks: page ranges whose dominant script is NOT the work's default,",
  "measured from the Vision output (Devanagari vs Kannada codepoint share per page).",
  "Sarvam takes one language per request, so a chunk must not straddle a block.",
  "These are contiguous front-matter prefaces and back-matter appendices, never",
  "interleaved. Sending them as sa-IN would make Sarvam disagree with Vision across",
  "~205 pages and push all of them to Gemini as if the OCR were bad."
 ],
